<title>SWITZERLAND: Adecco says pleased with Q1 result.</title>
<headline>Adecco says pleased with Q1 result.</headline>
<dateline>LAUSANNE, Switzerland 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Adecco SA, Europe's largest job recruitment group created through the merger of Swiss Adia and France's Ecco, said it was very pleased with its first quarter result, which proves that it was a correct to quickly integrate the two firms.</p>
<p>Although Adecco posted a net loss of 68.7 million Swiss francs ($46.9 million) for the first quarter, the company said profit before goodwill amortisation was the most important financial figure in order to judge the performance of Adecco because it shows the ability to finance further growth and to pay a dividend.</p>
<p>($ = 1.464 Swiss Francs)</p>
</text>
